+
+**Deliverables (branch `physics-loop/admissibility-induced-law-block27-unsoldered-formation-law-weak-coupling-causal-coupling-contracts-20260916`, independent PR against `main` at `6dda46fc1a`; parent on `main`: block 01):** the note `docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_UNSOLDERED_FORMATION_LAW_WEAK_COUPLING_THE_CAUSAL_COUPLING_CONTRACTS_ONE_INVARIANT_LAW_AND_EXPONENTIAL_LOSS_OF_MEMORY_BELOW_ONE_OVER_ROOT_THREE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-16.md`; the runner `scripts/admissibility_rule_unsoldered_formation_law_weak_coupling_causal_coupling_contracts_one_invariant_law_2026_09_16.py` (16 checks, 10 mutations, exact, under a second); the pinned cache; the control (`specs/supervisor_control_block27.py`) and the refuting pass (`specs/supervisor_control_block27_refuter.py`) with outputs; `GOAL_block27.md`; `CHECKER_block27_findings.md`; this record. Blocks 06–26 remain open as PRs #8034, #8035, #8138–#8142, #8146–#8158, #8168, #8170.
+
+**Why this block.** The twelve-hour continuation after block 26: the weak-coupling side of the sphere formation law was the proof-shaped remainder and the last empty cell of the campaign's table of explicit uniqueness regions (six-axis static, block 03; six-axis formation, block 08; sphere static, block 21).
+
+## Result, in one paragraph
+The sphere kernel's total-variation sensitivity to its predecessor sum is at most `1/(2√3)` per unit: the density's log-derivative is `s − A(κ)û`, the directional second moment is `A/κ + (1 − 3A/κ − A²)(û·d)²`, and the coefficient of the angle is non-positive because `A(κ)/κ` is decreasing — a series comparison of `2 sinh² κ` with `(κ/2) sinh 2κ + κ²` whose `κ²` terms cancel and whose higher coefficients are `(2^{2m}/(2m)!)(m/2 − 1) ≥ 0` (T1). Coupling two runs from different initial planes site by site with a near-optimal coupling of the two kernels, the per-site expected chordal distance obeys `D_{t+1} ≤ √3β D_t`; for `β < 1/√3` this gives exactly one invariant law, invariant under all rotations, reached from every initial plane within `2(√3β)^t` per site (T2), and the aligned plane's magnetization obeys `m_t ≤ (√3β)^t` (T3; on one site exactly `A(3β)^t ≤ β^t`). The route cannot reach beyond `β = 1` because the kernel's mean alone moves by a third of a small change (T4); its exact total-variation version would stop at `2/3` (the sensitivity is `1/4` at `V = 0` and numerically never larger). Block 26's runs lose the memory at every coupling tried, so `1/√3` is the route's constant, not a threshold. The four-way table of explicit weak-coupling uniqueness regions is complete.
+
+## Certificate
+- Runner: `TOTAL: PASS=16 FAIL=0`; 10 mutations each in its family; no floating-point literal or conversion; authors' names only in the allowed sections.
+- Control: the series coefficients (`0, 0, 2/45, 2/315, …`), the identities symbolically, the total-variation bound against quadrature (`0.2499` per unit over `300` random pairs against `0.2887`), the magnetization at `β = 0.3, 0.5` on `256 × 256` (below `10⁻²` by levels `4` and `7`, near `β^t`, inside `(√3β)^t`).
+- Refuting pass (`CHECKER_block27_findings.md`): two runs from antipodal planes coupled by the maximal (overlap) coupling built by rejection from the densities — the per-site distance contracts by `0.33–0.38` per level at `β = 0.3`, `0.51–0.57` at `0.5`, `0.58–0.65` at `0.577`, all inside `√3β = 0.52, 0.87, 1.00`; the total-variation sensitivity by Monte Carlo (`0.2509` maximum over `40` pairs); the one-site chain against `A(3β)^t`; near `V = 0` the mean difference per unit is `0.3333` and `2·TV` per unit `0.4999`. One tooling slip folded: the refuter's sampler degenerated at exactly zero concentration (a uniform draw was needed), caught by the `V = 0` check itself.
+- Claim type `bounded_theorem`; status `bounded-support`; trace `upstream_support`; audit required.
+
+## Not claimed
+That `1/√3` bounds where memory is kept (block 26 says it is lost at every coupling tried; a proof at strong coupling is open); other menus, orders or readings; any reading, menu, rule or coupling as physical.
